---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Lumen handles data: on-device processing, explicit consent, no sharing without permission."
  lang="en"
  altHref="/privacy/"
>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    This page explains, in plain language, how Lumen handles your data. It does not replace a full
    legal notice.
  </p>

  <div class="notice">
    This is a plain-language summary, not a legal document. A complete, GDPR-compliant privacy
    notice is pending legal review and will be published separately before any public release of the
    app.
  </div>

  <h2>On-device processing</h2>
  <p>
    Lumen's essential features work entirely on the phone, with no network connection. No audio or
    image captured by the camera or microphone ever leaves the device unless you explicitly choose
    to share it.
  </p>

  <h2>Explicit consent</h2>
  <p>
    Any feature that involves sharing data, for example with a family member or caregiver through
    the Family module, requires explicit consent that can be revoked at any time. Face recognition in
    the Remember module, once available, will only work with the explicit consent of the people
    recognized, and only on-device.
  </p>

  <h2>Optional server</h2>
  <p>
    An optional server (<a href="https://github.com/lumen-assistive/lumen-server">lumen-server</a>)
    allows syncing with caregivers only if voluntarily enabled. Data sent to the server is encrypted
    before it leaves the device: the server cannot read its contents.
  </p>

  <h2>Medical and emergency data</h2>
  <p>
    Lumen's medical and emergency features assist but do not replace a doctor or the 112 emergency
    number, and Lumen is not a certified medical device.
  </p>
</Layout>
